    q: "How does a year-end CAM reconciliation work, and how can it distort a property's trailing numbers?",
    a: "Tenants pay monthly estimates of their recoveries, based on the landlord's budget. After year-end, the landlord compares actual recoverable costs with what each tenant paid, then bills the shortfall or credits the overpayment. Because the true-up is billed months later, a T-12 can include last year's reconciliation or miss this year's, overstating or understating recovery income.",
