    a: "Physical occupancy is the share of units, or space, with a tenant in it. Economic occupancy is the share of potential rent actually collected: rent received divided by gross potential rent at market. It runs lower because it also subtracts below-market leases, concessions, bad debt and units that earn nothing, like models. Economic occupancy is what pays the bills.",
